#doc (Manual) "Galois groups" =>

This chapter lists the LMFDB definitions relating to *Galois groups*, migrated from the LaTeX blueprint. Each definition links back to its LMFDB knowl. The definitions from this area that the number field, elliptic curve and modular form chapters depend on are in the Background chapter instead.

:::definition "gg.arithmetically_equivalent" (lean := "MulAction.arithmeticallyEquivalentCount, Subgroup.arithmeticallyEquivalentSiblings, MulAction.arithmeticallyEquivalentCount_eq, Subgroup.IsGassmannEquivalent, Subgroup.IsGassmannEquivalent.index_eq")
*Arithmetically equivalent siblings.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.arithmetically_equivalent))

If $`K` is a {bpref "nf.degree"}[degree] $`n` {bpref "nf"}[number field] whose Galois closure has {bpref "nf.galois_group"}[Galois group] $`G\leq S_n`, then $`K` may have {bpref "nf.arithmetically_equivalent"}[arithmetically equivalent] fields.  The number of these is a function of $`G`.

Inside $`G`, we have $`H_1`, the stabilizer {bpref "group.subgroup"}[subgroup] of $`1`.  By the Galois correspondence, an arithmetically equivalent field corresponds to a conjugacy class of subgroups with representative $`H_2` such that

$$`|H_1 \cap C| = |H_2\cap C|`

for every {bpref "gg.conjugacy_classes"}[conjugacy class] $`C` of $`G`.

Depends on: {uses "gg.conjugacy_classes"}[] {uses "group.subgroup"}[] {uses "nf"}[] {uses "nf.arithmetically_equivalent"}[] {uses "nf.degree"}[] {uses "nf.galois_group"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.concentrated" (lean := "Subgroup.IsConcentrated, Subgroup.minPermIndexElements, Equiv.Perm.permIndex")
*Concentrated group.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.concentrated))

A transitive permutation {bpref "group"}[group] $`G` is *concentrated* if the subgroup of $`G` generated by all elements of minimal {bpref "gg.index"}[index] is a {bpref "group.proper_subgroup"}[proper] subgroup of $`G`.

Depends on: {uses "gg.index"}[] {uses "group"}[] {uses "group.proper_subgroup"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.conjugacy_classes" (lean := "ConjClasses, Equiv.Perm.cycleType, Equiv.Perm.cycleType_conj, Equiv.Perm.isConj_iff_cycleType_eq")
*Conjugacy class.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.conjugacy_classes))

{bpref "group.conjugacy_class"}[]  If $`G\leq S_n`, then all elements in the conjugacy class of an element have the same cycle type.

Depends on: {uses "group.conjugacy_class"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.degree" (lean := "Polynomial.natDegree, Polynomial.Gal.galActionHom, Polynomial.card_rootSet_eq_natDegree")
*Degree.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.degree))

A {bpref "gg.galois_group"}[Galois group] of an irreducible polynomial $`f(x)` is a transitive subgroup of $`S_n`, well-defined up to conjugation.  Its *degree* is $`n=\deg(f)`.

Depends on: {uses "gg.galois_group"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.elusive_group" (lean := "Subgroup.IsElusive, Subgroup.isElusive_map_permCongrHom_iff, Subgroup.isElusive_map_conj_iff, derangements")
*Elusive group.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.elusive_group))

An *elusive group* is a transitive permutation group $`H\leq S_n` with no fixed-point-free elements of prime order.
:::

:::definition "gg.field_automorphisms" (lean := "IsGalois.card_aut_fixedField_stabilizer, IsGalois.normalizerQuotientEquivAut, Subgroup.exists_isGalois_range_eq, IsGalois.normalClosure_fixedField_stabilizer, AdjoinRoot.card_aut_eq_card_rootSet")
*Field automorphisms associated with a Galois group.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.field_automorphisms))

Let $`G` be a transitive subgroup of $`S_n` and $`G_1=\{\sigma\in G \subset S_n \mid \sigma(1)=1\}`. The group $`G \subset S_n` can be realized as the {bpref "gg.galois_group"}[Galois group] of a field extension $`L/K`. Let $`F \subset L` be the fixed field of $`G_1` defined by the Galois action of $`G`, i.e., $`F = \{ a \in L \mid \forall g \in G_1,\, g(a) = a \}`. Then, $`F/K` is a field extension of degree $`n` whose Galois closure is $`L/K`.

Although $`F` might not be Galois over $`K`, one can consider the group {bpref "lf.automorphism_group"}[$`\Aut(F/K)`].

The group $`\Aut(F/K)` can be computed via the Galois correspondence. Group-theoretically, the order $`\# \Aut(F/K)` equals the order of the {bpref "group.centralizer"}[centralizer] of $`G` in $`S_n`.

If $`F/K` is realized as the extension $`F = K[x]/(f(x))` for some polynomial $`f(x) \in K[x]` then, the order $`\#\Aut(F/K)` is the number of roots of $`f(x)` in $`F`.

Depends on: {uses "gg.galois_group"}[] {uses "group.centralizer"}[] {uses "lf.automorphism_group"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.generic_polynomial"
*Generic polynomial.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.generic_polynomial))

Let $`K` be a {bpref "ring.field"}[field] and $`G` a finite {bpref "group"}[group], $`t_1, \ldots, t_n` and $`x` indeterminants.  A polynomial $`f(t_1,\ldots,t_n,x)\in K(t_1,\ldots,t_n)[x]` is *generic* for G if

 1. the splitting field $`L` of $`f` is {bpref "nf.is_galois"}[Galois] and {bpref "gg.regular_extension"}[regular] over $`K(t_1,\ldots,t_n)`
 2. $`\Gal(L/K(t_1,\ldots,t_n))\cong G`
 3. every Galois extension $`E/K` with $`\Gal(E/K)\cong G` is the splitting field of $`f(a_1,\ldots,a_n,x)` for some $`(a_1,\ldots,a_n)\in K^n`
 4. condition 3 holds for every extension field of $`K`.

Depends on: {uses "gg.regular_extension"}[] {uses "group"}[] {uses "nf.is_galois"}[] {uses "ring.field"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.group_action_invariants" (lean := "MulAction.IsPreprimitive, alternatingGroup, IntermediateField, Polynomial.natDegree, TauCeti.isPreprimitive_iff_isAtom_adjoin_simple, Polynomial.Gal.sign")
*Group action Invariants.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.group_action_invariants))

If a group $`G` acts transitively on an $`n` element set, the action is isomorphic to the natural action of a transitive subgroup of $`S_n`.  In terms of the Galois correspondence, we consider an irreducible separable polynomial $`f(x)\in K[x]`, let $`F` be a field obtained by adjoining a root of $`f(x)` to $`K` and suppose $`G` is the Galois group of the splitting field of $`f(x)` over $`K` where the action on the roots of $`f(x)`, $`\alpha_1, \ldots, \alpha_n` is through the subscripts.

The *degree* is $`n`, the number of elements in the set which equals $`\deg(f)=[F:K]`.

Transitive subgroups of $`S_n` have been classified and numbered; $`t` is the corresponding number assigned to this group.

The *parity* is $`1` if $`G` is a subgroup of $`A_n`, otherwise it is $`-1`.

The action is *primitive* if the only block of size larger than 1 for the action is the whole set.  In terms of the Galois correspondence, the action of $`G` is primitive if and only if $`F/K` has no proper intermediate fields.

*Resolvent fields* are other fields inside the splitting field of $`f(x)` over $`K`.  These correspond to small index subgroups of $`G`,up to conjugation.  For a degree $`m` field $`E`, the action of $`G` on the embeddings of $`E` into the splitting field of $`f(x)` gives a transitive group action, which is faithful for the appropriate quotient of $`G`.  These are given in terms of the degree of the normal closure of $`E`, and information describing the faithful transitive group action corresponding to $`E`.
:::

:::definition "gg.index" (lean := "TauCeti.orbitCount, Equiv.Perm.isLeast_card_sub_orbitCount, Equiv.Perm.partition")
*Index of a permuation.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.index))

If $`\sigma\in S_n`, its *index* is

$$`\textrm{ind}(\sigma) = n - \text{number of cycles}`

for the full disjoint cycle decomposition of $`\sigma`.
:::

:::definition "gg.int_modules" (lean := "Representation, Representation.asModule, TauCeti.IsIndecomposableModule")
*Indecomposable integral representation.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.int_modules))

If $`G` is a finite group, an *integral representation* of $`G` is a homomorphism $`\rho\colon G\to\Aut(\Z^r)` for some $`r\in\Z`, $`r> 0`.

The representation $`\rho` is *indecomposable* if it is not equivalent to the direct sum of integral representations.
:::

:::definition "gg.invariants" (lean := "Nat.card, IsCyclic, IsMulCommutative, IsSolvable, TauCeti.characterTable")
*Group invariants.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.invariants))

The *order* of $`G` is its number of elements.

It is *cyclic* if and only if there exists $`g\in G` such that $`G=\langle g\rangle`, the cyclic subgroup generated by $`g`.

It is *abelian* if and only if $`xy=yx` for all $`x,y\in G`.

It is *solvable* if and only if there is a series of subgroups

$$`\langle e\rangle = G_0 \leq G_1 \leq \cdots \leq G_n=G`

such that each $`G_i` is normal in $`G_{i+1}` and all quotients $`G_{i+1}/G_i` are abelian.

The *character table* shows values of all characters of irreducible complex representations of $`G`.  The rows are indexed by characters, and the columns by conjugacy classes of $`G`.
:::

:::definition "gg.label"
*Galois group label.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.label))

Labels for Galois groups are of the form $`\tt{nTt}` where $`n` is the {bpref "gg.degree"}[degree] and $`t` is the {bpref "gg.tnumber"}[$`T`-number].

Depends on: {uses "gg.degree"}[] {uses "gg.tnumber"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.malle_a" (lean := "Subgroup.malleA, Subgroup.minPermIndex, Subgroup.malleA_bot, Equiv.Perm.permIndex")
*Malle's constant $`a(G)`.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.malle_a))

If $`G` is a {bpref "group.subgroup"}[subgroup] of $`S_n`, *Malle's constant* is defined as

$$`a(G)=\frac{1}{\min(\{\textrm{ind}(g) \mid e\neq g\in G\})}`

where $`\textrm{ind}(g)` is the {bpref "gg.index"}[index] of the element $`g`.  Note, if $`G` is the trivial group, $`a(G)` is defined to be $`0`.

This constant appears in the conjectures of Malle on asymptotics for the number of number fields with a given Galois group $`G\leq S_n` , .

Depends on: {uses "gg.index"}[] {uses "group.subgroup"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.malle_b" (lean := "Subgroup.malleB, Subgroup.minPermIndexElements, IsRationallyConj, RatConjClasses")
*Malle's constant $`b(G)`.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.malle_b))

Let $`G` be a {bpref "group.subgroup"}[subgroup] of $`S_n` and $`\mathrm{CL}_{\Q}(G)` the collection of {bpref "group.division"}[rational conjugacy classes] of $`G`.

*Malle's constant $`b(G)`*  is defined to be

$$`b(G)=\# \{ C \in \mathrm{CL}_{\Q}(G) : \textrm{ind}(C) = a(G)^{-1}\}`

where $`\textrm{ind}(C)` is the {bpref "gg.index"}[index] of $`C`. Here $`a(G)` is {bpref "gg.malle_a"}[Malle's constant $`a(G)`], so that $`b(G)` is the number of non-identity rational conjugacy classes of $`G` of minimal index.

These constants appear in the conjectures of Malle on asymptotics for the number of number fields with a given Galois group $`G\leq S_n` , .

Depends on: {uses "gg.index"}[] {uses "gg.malle_a"}[] {uses "group.division"}[] {uses "group.subgroup"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.other_representations" (lean := "Subgroup.IsSibling, IntermediateField.isSibling_fixedField_iff_isSibling, IntermediateField.isSibling_fixedField_iff, Algebra.IsSibling, Subgroup.normalCore")
*Siblings for a Galois group.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.other_representations))

An abstract group $`G` may be a transitive subgroup of $`S_n` for different $`n` and even in different (non-conjugate) ways for a given $`n`.  Each action is identified by a label of the form "'nTt"' where $`n` is the {bpref "gg.degree"}[degree] and "'t"' is the T-number classifying the action.

In terms of the Galois correspondence, the group $`G` corresponds to a degree $`n` extension $`F/K` where $`F=K(\alpha)`, and $`G` is the Galois group of the splitting field of the monic irreducible polynomial for $`\alpha`.  The *siblings* correspond to {bpref "nf.sibling"}[sibling fields], which are not isomorphic to $`F`, yet have the same normal closure.

There can be more than one action with the same transitive classification.  This corresponds to non-isomorphic fields with the same degree, Galois group, and Galois closure.  We indicate multiplicity using the notation """nTt x k""" where there are "'k"' non-conjugate subgroups such that the action is "'nTt"'.

Depends on: {uses "gg.degree"}[] {uses "nf.sibling"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.parity" (lean := "alternatingGroup, Equiv.Perm.sign, Polynomial.Gal.sign")
*Parity of a Galois group.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.parity))

A {bpref "gg.galois_group"}[Galois group] $`G\leq S_n` has *parity* $`1` if $`G\leq A_n`, and $`-1` otherwise.

Depends on: {uses "gg.galois_group"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.primitive" (lean := "MulAction.IsPreprimitive, MulAction.isCoatom_stabilizer_iff_preprimitive, TauCeti.isPreprimitive_iff_isAtom_adjoin_simple")
*Primitivity of a Galois group.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.primitive))

Let $`G` be a transitive subgroup of $`S_n`.  Then $`G` is *primitive* if, under the Galois correspondence, it corresponds to a field with no non-trivial proper subfields.

An equivalent group-theoretic condition is as follows.  Let

$$`G_1 = \{\sigma\in G\mid \sigma(1)=1\}.`

Then $`G` is primitive if and only if $`G_1` is a maximal subgroup of $`G`.
:::

:::definition "gg.regular_extension" (lean := "algebraicClosure, IsIntegrallyClosedIn")
*Regular extension.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.regular_extension))

Let $`t_1, \ldots, t_n` be indeterminants over a field $`K`.  A Galois extension $`L/K(t_1, \ldots t_n)` is *regular* if every element of $`L-K` is transcendental over $`K`.
:::

:::definition "gg.resolvents"
*Resolvents of a Galois group.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.resolvents))

Let $`K/F` is finite {bpref "nf.separable"}[separable] extension of fields with {bpref "nf.galois_closure"}[Galois closure] $`L` and let let $`G= \Gal(L/F)`.  Then any subfield of $`L` is a resolvent field for $`K/F`.  These are in bijection with the subgroups of $`G`.

One way to group these fields is to collect together subfields with the same Galois closure since given one such field, the other fields are in a collection are visible as {bpref "gg.other_representations"}[siblings] of the field.  A natural representative of such a collection would be a field of minimal {bpref "nf.degree"}[degree] over $`F` with ties broken by taking a field whose Galois closure has {bpref "gg.galois_group"}[Galois group] $`nTj` with minimal {bpref "gg.tnumber"}[$`j`].

In group theoretic terms, $`G\leq S_n` where $`n=[K:F]`.  The *resolvents* of $`G` correspond to quotients $`G/N` where $`N \unlhd G`.  For each normal {bpref "group.subgroup"}[subgroup] $`N`, we then look for $`H\leq G` such that the {bpref "group.core"}[core] of $`H` equals $`N`, and then pick the subgroup $`H` of minimal {bpref "group.subgroup.index"}[index] in $`G` so that when $`G` acts transitively on the $`m` left cosets of $`H` by left translation, the {bpref "gg.tnumber"}[T-number] of the permutation reputation is minimized.

The fixed field of $`H` is then a {bpref "nf.stem_field"}[stem field] for $`L^N`, the fixed field of $`N` over $`F`.  The Galois group for $`L^N/F` has is a subgroup of $`S_m`, up to conjugation.

Depends on: {uses "gg.galois_group"}[] {uses "gg.other_representations"}[] {uses "group.core"}[] {uses "group.subgroup"}[] {uses "group.subgroup.index"}[] {uses "nf.degree"}[] {uses "nf.galois_closure"}[] {uses "nf.separable"}[] {uses "nf.stem_field"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.semiconcentrated" (lean := "Subgroup.IsSemiconcentrated, Subgroup.minPermIndexElements, Equiv.Perm.permIndex")
*Semiconcentrated group.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.semiconcentrated))

A transitive permutation {bpref "group"}[group] $`G` is *semiconcentrated* if there exists an element of minimal {bpref "gg.index"}[index] so that the minimal normal subgroup containing it is a {bpref "group.proper_subgroup"}[proper] subgroup of $`G`.

Depends on: {uses "gg.index"}[] {uses "group"}[] {uses "group.proper_subgroup"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.subfields" (lean := "IntermediateField, TauCeti.rootBlockIntermediateFieldOrderIso")
*Subfields.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.subfields))

In terms of the Galois correspondence, a transitive group $`G\leq S_n` is the Galois group of an irreducible degree $`n` polynomial $`f(x)\in K[x]`.  Let $`F=K(\alpha)` where $`\alpha` is a root of $`f(x)`.  Then the *subfields* are intermediate fields for the extension $`F/K`.
:::

:::definition "gg.subnormal_series" (lean := "Subgroup.SubnormalSeries, Subgroup.IsSubnormal, Subgroup.isSubnormal_iff_exists_subnormalSeries")
*Subnormal series.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.subnormal_series))

A *subnormal series* of a group $`G` is a chain of subgroups,

$$`\langle e\rangle = H_0 \leq H_i \leq \cdots \leq H_{n} =G`

where each $`H_i` is a normal subgroup of $`H_{i+1}`.
:::

:::definition "gg.tnumber"
*$`T`-number of a transitive group.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.tnumber))

The transitive subgroups of $`S_n` have been classified, up to conjugation, for small values of $`n`, including all $`n\leq 47`.  The ordering is weakly increasing by the {bpref "group.order"}[order] of the {bpref "group"}[group].  The $`T`-number of a subgroup is its index in this classification.

An algorithm for generating the classification is given in , and the results can be accessed from the computer algebra systems SageMath, GAP, and Magma.

Depends on: {uses "group"}[] {uses "group.order"}[]
:::

:::definition "gg.transitivity" (lean := "MulAction.IsMultiplyPretransitive")
*Transitivity number.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/gg.transitivity))

If a {bpref "group"}[group] $`G` acts on a set $`A` of order $`n` and $`k\leq n`, then $`G` is *$`k`-transitive* if it acts {bpref "group.action"}[transitively] on the set

$$`S=\{(a_1,\ldots,a_k)\in A^k \mid a_i \text{ are distinct}\}.`

The largest such value $`k` is the *transitivity number* of the action.

Depends on: {uses "group"}[] {uses "group.action"}[]
:::
